{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1026","t":"Many thanks kkb for you reply and notes. That helps a lot. I will need to practice many more. Thankyou","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1026","p":42,"im":[],"m":1026},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1027","t":"Another try. Any comments\n\nwelcome","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1027","p":42,"im":["8fc49009fa2a44772f592c45427a98ed3f18b488"],"m":1027},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1028","t":"OK, I've done a lot of practice with CP today and think I'm understanding how all this stuff fits together a little better. I've marked up a chart with CP and some explanations for price movements. I'd like to hear some feedback and/or criticism. PS. Hope my chart is not too busy","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1028","p":42,"im":["1a134bb650b072ab34d23de2c271d9f25e774a55","a86da21f25cb8e70c11d114087395483012d1b57"],"m":1028},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1029","t":"Another try at CP","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1029","p":42,"im":["a206feaf55f735e8938a30b797facfd0093c951d"],"m":1029},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1030","t":"So here's a compression of GBPUSD in the WKLY TF.\n\nIt looks spot on to me. But I just want to dive into a closer look into this data and see how I could have taken advantage of this series of PA.\n\nHere's the same data on the Daily TF\n\nWhat do you guys think?","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#1030","p":42,"im":[],"m":1030},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1031","t":"Hi Projetct,\n\nNice Analysis. I spotted a QM on the 4 hour which would have made for a nice entry.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1031","p":42,"im":["a6b614699b93389ad08c800d87b1529d1f08cbdf"],"m":1031},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1032","t":"Generally you are correct:)\n\nOnly one thing (on chart).\n\nastro wrote: OK, I've done a lot of practice with CP today and think I'm understanding how all this stuff fits together a little better. I've marked up a chart with CP and some explanations for price movements. I'd like to hear some feedback and/or criticism. PS. Hope my chart is not too busy","a":"kkb","d":"","n":"#1032","p":42,"im":["42a2645b4b6511eda7104502e1da9993604fc8c1","f187184768beee2d870e46eff67d07d88c2daf4d","1a134bb650b072ab34d23de2c271d9f25e774a55"],"m":1032},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1033","t":"I'm very interested in gaining my understanding in identifying when a compression is occuring and what is most likely to happen next when they appear.\n\nHere's another in-depth study of compression.\n\nPlease do correct me if there is a flaw in my thinking when looking at these chart. Thanks","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#1033","p":42,"im":[],"m":1033},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1034","t":"Thanks KKB for your detailed reply... makes a lot of sense. I've been thinking about your response regarding Ignored Supply/Demand and I think something has just clicked. Just want to confirm if I could.\n\nSo you're saying that S/D being exhausted is a similar concept to S/D being ignored. So price did react to the supply, but couldn't continue lower indicating that sellers were exhausted. So when price shoots up thru supply this creates a FTR. But basically regardless, we can expect the same reaction. Hope this makes sense.\n\nI will do lots more practice this week and hopefully will be able to spot these things.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1034","p":42,"im":[],"m":1034},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1035","t":"All looks good to me Project:)","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1035","p":42,"im":[],"m":1035},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1036","t":"astro wrote: All looks good to me Project:)\n\nThanks astro, I'm beginning to see the market in the IT's perspective little by little. From my opinion the ITs profit large amount of pips and quickly too when they set up a price compression.","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#1036","p":42,"im":[],"m":1036},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1037","t":"projectsagana wrote:\n\nastro wrote: All looks good to me Project:)\n\nThat must be a fantastic feeling. Well done. I believe I'm following close behind you.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1037","p":42,"im":[],"m":1037},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1038","t":"More CP homework","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1038","p":42,"im":["6026309649a0238bbf3bb43d417af14b365cac07"],"m":1038},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1039","t":"astro wrote: More CP homework","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#1039","p":42,"im":["6026309649a0238bbf3bb43d417af14b365cac07"],"m":1039},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1040","t":"Thanks Project for pointing those out A couple more.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1040","p":42,"im":["d2064c9f7b22549f46032c10856b8b1499cb9942","a96fc31bfdcce0de5395b31d812e0e37f6e8c6b1"],"m":1040},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1041","t":"Yes. In my opinion S/D being exhausted and S/D being ignored means, that there is no sell/buy orders in the S/D zone. In my opinion if we, lets say, have supply zone, then price couldn't go through it if there are still orders in it (it can't be ignored).\n\nBut note that it is only my opionion and I could be wrong. Maybe some great people from this forum could comment that:)\n\nastro wrote: Thanks KKB for your detailed reply... makes a lot of sense. I've been thinking about your response regarding Ignored Supply/Demand and I think something has just clicked. Just want to confirm if I could.\n\nSo you're saying that S/D being exhausted is a similar concept to S/D being ignored. So price did react to the supply, but couldn't continue lower indicating that sellers were exhausted. So when price shoots up thru supply this creates a FTR. But basically regardless, we can expect the same reaction. Hope this makes sense.\n\nI will do lots more practice this week and hopefully will be able to spot these things.","a":"kkb","d":"","n":"#1041","p":42,"im":[],"m":1041},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1042","t":"","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1042","p":42,"im":["9521c213b1cf77149ee91bc179903d73fdbcf511"],"m":1042},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1043","t":"More CP homework","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1043","p":42,"im":["e2f9d46ad60fe2549e197b23f0c8b3d1f5a30db5","ab8c8f3dde2bb67b03e82b9a22af289f80609ed2","a6aaa5a21e247729007200f746dfc7995aea644c","6a06309f538bf88034d941550d31222eea78a47e"],"m":1043},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1044","t":"astro wrote: More CP homework\n\nEverything looks great but just made this one correction. Anybody is also free to comments on these.\n\nOther than that good job!","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#1044","p":42,"im":["ab8c8f3dde2bb67b03e82b9a22af289f80609ed2"],"m":1044},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1045","t":"Thanks for your comments Project. it means a lot to get good feedback. Thanks for pointing out the Can Can setup. this is something I've read about but have yet to start my homework on. I think I'm inspired to get started on learning about the Can Can now that I have a good understanding of RBD, DBR and compression.\n\nThanks also for pointing out the flip zone. I was I guess i hadn't thought of using the term Flip Zone for this type of move. Usually only for RDB and DBR, but I see the logic in this now. It's something I knew happened quite regularly but wasn't sure how to classify it. thanks for helping me develop a deeper understanding of all this.:)","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1045","p":42,"im":[],"m":1045},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1046","t":"So far with my CP homework, I haven't included CP + LQ. So will start to post a few of theses. Comments welcome.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1046","p":42,"im":["e016396043059a11bd3433ce70f2e5a0f936ef88","2a642c46fe755c50fed5da5180c206a44c81a785","6fce30742644882a94f52d37ea8bb18e5b6e4997"],"m":1046},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1047","t":"Another CP + LQ","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#1047","p":42,"im":["ce39dd8cea968879aadd531c579fbb5810718c84"],"m":1047},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1048","t":"Hello everyone, this is my work on compression believe that I am on the right way. Thanks so much in advance.","a":"click","d":"","n":"#1048","p":42,"im":["1329746978ec924384d595dda57ba63616d6b1e4"],"m":1048},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1049","t":"That's my Compression vision... i hope it's all right","a":"juniormaiafx","d":"","n":"#1049","p":42,"im":["6812d46507353a9006d1f34341fa818009bcf1c3","118967e85c08cb1f6d2491a0f771879951f1876c","fe6aba61bbea14124970ddd84d22467b8047419a","d7b1fbd9fdb888092049c33693d310bc18fb3c4f","9f76341bae3447b25d5ba14146046d16f87db7e7","40d44843073e916d7faaa93fa19edc8a926ddec5","f6a1979e8e2783e4d624e7ccdfb78658eaf314fe","3d0985c666b94c6c52379e4b816e67864ac406ba"],"m":1049},{"id":"aboutcompression_p42_1050","t":"Good day to you all\n\nI'm starting Homework n°2 which is Compressions. I think I understood the concept, and here is my first attempt at telling the story of a CP.\n\nQuestion for Teachers/Masters: just for my information (I know it is about reading and not trading, at the moment, but) where would have been the entry and stoploss? Is the entry at the close of the Engulf candle (the one I'm talking about on the right) or before? Would the stop be just above the high? Thank you for your precious help.","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1050","p":42,"im":["3815f06c5254194f2c485ab715b81b89d48195e6"],"m":1050}],"images":[{"k":"8fc49009fa2a44772f592c45427a98ed3f18b488","t":"assets/thumbs/8fc49009fa2a44772f592c45427a98ed3f18b488.webp","f":"assets/images/8fc49009fa2a44772f592c45427a98ed3f18b488.jpeg","w":1364,"h":734,"b":75889,"o":"8fc49009fa2a44772f592c45427a98ed3f18b488.jpeg","p":42,"pid":"aboutcompression_p42_1027"},{"k":"1a134bb650b072ab34d23de2c271d9f25e774a55","t":"assets/thumbs/1a134bb650b072ab34d23de2c271d9f25e774a55.webp","f":"assets/images/1a134bb650b072ab34d23de2c271d9f25e774a55.jpeg","w":1366,"h":738,"b":109714,"o":"1a134bb650b072ab34d23de2c271d9f25e774a55.jpeg","p":42,"pid":"aboutcompression_p42_1032"},{"k":"a86da21f25cb8e70c11d114087395483012d1b57","t":"assets/thumbs/a86da21f25cb8e70c11d114087395483012d1b57.webp","f":"assets/images/a86da21f25cb8e70c11d114087395483012d1b57.jpeg","w":1366,"h":738,"b":110266,"o":"a86da21f25cb8e70c11d114087395483012d1b57.jpeg","p":42,"pid":"aboutcompression_p42_1028"},{"